# Branches are conditional editorial routes, not measured best-in-slot allocations.
CLASSES={
 'warlock':dict(name='Warlock',start='Shadow Bolt',summary='Choose Affliction when you want damage-over-time kills to spread through a crowd. Choose Demonology when you want summons alongside your spells. A late-tree setup changes your opening spell; it is not the same character as a fresh Warlock.',
 routes=[['Affliction','Nightfall → Contagion → Siphon Life → Seed of Corruption','Corruption and Curse of Agony can pass on after a kill. DoT ticks provide healing through Siphon Life. Seed changes the opening spell to Corruption and adds death explosions.','A target must carry your damage-over-time effects; spreading needs a death. Sparse boss encounters do not supply the same chain of kills.'],['Demonology','Demonic Familiar and summon-related talents','An Imp and later summon choices put additional attackers beside you. Support the summon branch you have actually unlocked instead of drafting only for a distant capstone.','Summons and DoT healing are different engines. Owning a pet does not establish that every hit heals you.']],
 priority=['With only Shadow Bolt available, use an offered Corruption or Curse of Agony to establish the DoT engine before expecting propagation.','Once Contagion is active, favour damage over time that can remain on several enemies; move so afflicted enemies die near another target.','If incoming damage is the problem, check whether Siphon Life is actually allocated. More targets do not substitute for a missing healing talent.','With Seed selected, adapt around the Corruption start. Do not spend the opening waiting for the default Shadow Bolt to appear.'],
 fallback='If the spread branch has not opened, use the spells you receive to keep room to move; do not reserve the whole run for a final-tree effect. If packs clear but a boss stalls, prioritise the damage source that is actually hitting that boss rather than counting chain explosions that need adds.',
 mistake='Do not read “DoT healing” as 1% of your maximum health per tick. The inspected Siphon Life text describes healing from the tick’s damage. Exact rank-dependent damage values are omitted where the client exposes a template.'),
 'hunter':dict(name='Hunter',start='Auto Shot',summary='Use Marksmanship for an Aimed Shot route once its talents are available, or Beast Mastery for a pet-focused route. A fresh Hunter starts with Auto Shot; Kill Shot changes the start to Aimed Shot.',
 routes=[['Marksmanship','Piercing Shots → Rapid Fire → Kill Shot','Direct ranged attacks build toward Aimed Shot. Kill Shot changes the starting spell and lets a killing blow ready it again, with a two-second limit.','A kill-reset chain needs enemies you can finish. It is not an unlimited reset on every hit against an isolated boss.'],['Beast Mastery','Wolf-related talents → Bestial Wrath','Bestial Wrath adds a raptor beside your wolf and gives pet bites additional nearby hits.','The two-pet setup requires its talent investment. Do not assume a fresh character begins with the developed pair.']],
 priority=['Read the selected talent branch before choosing between shot and pet upgrades. The same class can have two different damage engines.','For Marksmanship, keep your current ranged attack useful while working toward Aimed Shot interactions; prioritise a relevant attack over an unrelated trap just because the trap is new.','For Beast Mastery, support the pet attacks you have unlocked, then add wave coverage when the offers allow it.','Keep a retreat route. If enemies reach you before they die, a movement or recovery choice can solve a problem that another conditional kill proc cannot.'],
 fallback='Without Kill Shot, plan around Auto Shot and the available ranged cards. Against a boss without adds, evaluate sustained hits rather than the best-looking chain of kill resets. Without the second pet, treat the current summon setup as one pet, not a failed copy of a finished build.',
 mistake='Do not copy the community reconstruction’s Arcane Shot opener into the original game. Starter changes, kill triggers and pet investment explain why two Hunter recordings may open differently.'),
 'priest':dict(name='Priest',start='Smite',summary='Choose Discipline when you need a shield-based survival route; choose Shadow when you want Shadow Word: Pain to spread after kills. The shield and damage-over-time routes depend on different talents and should not be merged into one automatic recipe.',
 routes=[['Discipline','Divine Aegis → Rapture → Penance','Divine Aegis changes the start to Power Word: Shield and adds damage when a shield breaks. Rapture can immediately raise a broken shield again, with a 15-second limit. Penance adds free casts.','A shield-break effect requires the shield to break. It is not the same as damage gained while a shield stays intact.'],['Shadow','Shadow Word: Pain support → Shadowform','Shadowform lasts for the run; a death with Shadow Word: Pain creates an explosion and passes the pain to the nearest enemy.','The propagation requires a death with the effect present. It does not prove that an isolated boss will die quickly.']],
 priority=['If repeated contact is ending runs, first check whether the shield-start milestone and reapplication talent are allocated.','Add damage that works while you move. A defensive setup still needs a spell capable of finishing enemies.','On Shadow, get Shadow Word: Pain functioning before taking choices whose value assumes its spread.','After the engine is working, use the actual failure point to choose health, recovery or damage; do not replace a shield problem with another conditional death explosion.'],
 fallback='Before the shield milestone is open, Smite remains the baseline start. Before Shadowform, treat Shadow Word: Pain as a DoT rather than guaranteed propagation. Do not spend future talent benefits in advance when deciding whether the present character can survive a harder zone.',
 mistake='Siphon Life belongs to the Warlock route described elsewhere. Do not assume a Priest gets the same per-tick healing merely because both classes use damage over time.'),
 'druid':dict(name='Druid',start='Wrath',summary='Choose Balance for repeated Starfire and ranged spell coverage. Choose Feral when you want a melee form route. Cat Form and Dire Bear Form exclude each other, so decide whether the present run needs offensive mobility or the bear route before investing.',
 routes=[['Balance','Omen of Clarity → Starfall → Force of Nature','Starfall adds a free Starfire every four seconds. Force of Nature adds two treants and changes the starting spell to Moonfire.','A default Wrath start and a Force of Nature Moonfire start represent different talent states; neither makes the other source automatically wrong.'],['Feral','Feral talents → Cat Form or Dire Bear Form','Cat Form increases offensive and movement stats and changes the start to Shred. The client explicitly makes Cat and Dire Bear mutually exclusive.','A melee form changes where your damage is delivered. Being able to take a form does not remove the need to survive contact.']],
 priority=['For Balance, establish the actual ranged damage engine first; select Starfire support when repeated Starfire is your chosen route.','Treat the treants as a late-tree addition unless Force of Nature is already active. Do not assume a fresh Druid has two summons.','For Feral, choose one form direction and support the spells it uses, rather than dividing limited choices between mutually exclusive endpoints.','If you cannot hold space around a pack, use control or recovery before another offensive modifier whose damage you cannot safely deliver.'],
 fallback='Without Starfall, do not calculate a free Starfire every four seconds. Without a form talent, keep the Wrath opening in mind when deciding what your first offered card must solve. A change in permanent talents is a better reason to change the route than a single unlucky offer.',
 mistake='Do not add Cat Form and Dire Bear bonuses together. Also keep the periodic free Starfire separate from ordinary Starfire cooldown upgrades; they are different sources of casts.'),
 'rogue':dict(name='Rogue',start='Sinister Strike',summary='Choose Combat for direct-hit spillover, Assassination for poison or bleed deaths, or Subtlety for a Backstab route. Rogue remains a melee choice: select an engine you can keep applying while preserving a way out of the crowd.',
 routes=[['Combat','Blade Flurry → Killing Spree','Blade Flurry sends Sinister Strike and Eviscerate hits into additional nearby enemies. Killing Spree adds targets and a free Sinister Strike every three seconds.','The direct attack must connect, and other enemies must be nearby. It is not a free ranged safety layer.'],['Assassination','Poison/bleed support → Toxic Bloom','Toxic Bloom turns deaths of poisoned or bleeding enemies into toxic clouds.','An unpoisoned, unbleeding kill does not satisfy the stated trigger; a large single target may not feed a death chain.'],['Subtlety','Backstab support → Shadow Dance','A separate damage direction for players building around Backstab rather than the default attack.','Do not automatically combine every Subtlety benefit with a Combat or poison route. Check the selected talent text.']],
 priority=['With a fresh Sinister Strike start, first make the attack you can actually deliver useful. A poison capstone cannot rescue an opening before it is allocated.','For Combat, prioritise the supported direct hits and multi-target interaction, then take survival that allows safe melee contact.','For Assassination, establish poison or bleed application before expecting Toxic Bloom to clear the crowd.','If elites die but small enemies surround you, invest in the relevant spread/nearby-hit engine. If contact kills you immediately, resolve survival before adding another trigger.'],
 fallback='When a desired spell does not appear, choose support for the engine you already have rather than spending every offer on a disconnected skill. Against an isolated boss, judge repeatable hits and recovery; a build’s best wave-clearing death chain may not be active.',
 mistake='Do not copy a developed character’s jewellery-dependent choice as a universal opening order. This guide compares talent triggers; it does not establish a best necklace drop or a guaranteed clear.'),
 'warrior':dict(name='Warrior',start='Cleave',summary='Choose Fury for repeated Whirlwind and damage-based recovery, or Protection for a health-and-shield route. Bladestorm and Titan change the start of a developed Warrior; a fresh Cleave character has to build toward those benefits.',
 routes=[['Fury','Rampage → Flurry → Blood Craze → Bladestorm','Rampage adds Whirlwinds on kills, Flurry adds repeat hits, and Blood Craze turns a share of damage into healing. Bladestorm starts with Whirlwind and adds free casts every three seconds.','Kill-based casts need kills. Damage-based healing needs damage delivered; it is not a fixed full-health refill.'],['Protection','Shield Slam support → Shockwave → Titan','Titan starts with Shield Slam, raises the damage-reduction ceiling and adds maximum-health scaling.','A maximum-health route and a direct Whirlwind route do not value every offer in the same way. Check the active branch before choosing.']],
 priority=['Before Bladestorm, maintain Cleave and choose usable wave damage rather than assuming the capstone is already casting for you.','With the Fury engine active, favour the attacks named by its talents. Do not add a separate attack only to fill every available choice.','When contact damage is the limiting factor, compare recovery that depends on your damage with the defensive route you can currently afford.','With Titan selected, evaluate health and supported Shield Slam effects together. Do not judge the build solely by a direct-damage number.'],
 fallback='A missing Whirlwind offer is less destructive once Bladestorm is active than it is on a fresh character. Before the capstone, pick for the present attack bar. If a boss has no adds, Rampage’s kill engine is not evidence of sustained boss output.',
 mistake='A starting-health number from an old reconstruction is not enough to rank a current original Warrior. Race, talents and permanent equipment also change the comparison.'),
 'paladin':dict(name='Paladin',start='Consecration',summary='Choose Protection when you want shields and maximum health to support damage, or Retribution when you are building around critical-triggered Exorcism. A default Consecration start differs from the Hammer of Justice start granted by the Protection route.',
 routes=[['Protection','Hallowed Ground → Ardent Defender → Hammer of the Righteous','Hammer of Justice can trigger Consecration; the shield route connects defence with damage. Hammer of the Righteous adds maximum-health scaling and a burst when a shield breaks.','Damage while shielded and damage on shield break are different conditions. Do not count both as permanently active.'],['Retribution','Critical-hit interactions → Divine Storm','A separate direction for Exorcism-related burst rather than the health-and-shield plan.','Critical-triggered effects need actual critical hits. A defensive gear setup does not automatically supply the offensive trigger rate.']],
 priority=['Check the opening spell after changing talents. If the shield branch changes it to Hammer of Justice, draft around that start.','For Protection, choose effects that keep the shield/health engine relevant before adding a disconnected damage branch.','For Retribution, establish the critical-hit and Exorcism interaction before evaluating more conditional burst.','If a run ends to sustained contact, compare recovery and shielding first. If the character survives but cannot finish a boss, invest in damage that reaches the boss.'],
 fallback='Without the shield-start milestone, Consecration is the baseline opening. A later-game retaliation example can depend on maximum health and permanent gear that a new character lacks. Take a survivable route now rather than copying an end-state allocation by name.',
 mistake='Do not replace the original’s start with an old reconstruction’s Hammer of Wrath. The documented Protection milestone changes the opening again, so always state the talent condition.'),
 'mage':dict(name='Mage',start='Fireball',summary='Choose Fire for kill-triggered explosions, Frost for control and a Water Elemental, or Arcane for repeated spell strikes. For a first Mage route, Frost offers a control-based plan; that is an editorial choice about the kit, not a measured win-rate ranking.',
 routes=[['Fire','Ignite → Hot Streak → Pyroclasm','Fire critical hits and repeated crits feed the route; Pyroclasm starts with Pyroblast and adds explosions when Fire spells kill enemies.','The death explosion needs a Fire killing blow and is limited to three triggers a second. Do not model unlimited chains.'],['Frost','Frost support → Summon Water Elemental','The capstone starts with Frostbolt instead of Fireball, adds an elemental and creates a free Frost Nova every eight seconds.','A fresh Mage does not inherit the capstone’s summon or periodic nova. Control is not a guarantee against every encounter.'],['Arcane','Arcane spell interactions → Arcane Power','A route for repeated Arcane attacks and extra-strike interactions.','Choose it for the attacks and talents you actually have; do not count Fire-kill explosions as an Arcane benefit.']],
 priority=['If you are still learning movement, choose a route that gives you room to deliver damage. A higher theoretical ceiling is useless when contact ends the run.','For Fire, establish Fire damage and critical interactions before expecting Pyroclasm to carry dense waves.','For Frost, distinguish ordinary Frostbolt upgrades from the summon and free-nova effects granted by the capstone.','After the chosen engine works, use the current failure point to choose health, control or damage. Do not draft three competing schools without a reason.'],
 fallback='Before a capstone changes the opener, use the default Fireball start in your plan. Against a boss without nearby enemies, evaluate sustained casts rather than wave-chain explosions. A missing offensive offer can be a reason to take survival, not to abandon every existing synergy.',
 mistake='A Frostbolt opening can be correct for a Water Elemental character and wrong as a universal statement about every Mage. Always record the selected talents when comparing runs.'),
}

def class_page(key):
 d=CLASSES[key];name=d['name']; rows=[[r[0],r[1],r[2],r[3]] for r in d['routes']]
 parts=[('choose','Choose the route for your current character',para('These are conditional routes assembled from the original client’s talent descriptions. Check prerequisites and the points you have already spent in the game before following an endpoint. '+ref('game'))+table(['Route','Talents to inspect','What makes it work','Condition that changes the choice'],rows)),
 ('draft','What to prioritise during the run',steps(d['priority'])+para('This is an editorial choice order, not a guaranteed card sequence. The offered upgrades and your current permanent investment still determine which step is available. '+ref('game'))),
 ('fallback','When the intended build is not ready',para(d['fallback'])+para('Before changing the whole plan, identify the failure: no room to move, too little recovery, or too little damage on the target. Change the part that addresses that failure, then compare another run with similar talents and equipment.')),
 ('check','Check the starter and trigger before copying a build',para('<strong>Baseline starter: '+d['start']+'.</strong> Talents can replace it; use the route conditions above rather than treating this as the opening for every developed character. '+ref('game'))+para(d['mistake'])+para('Record the game version, zone, difficulty, selected capstone, permanent equipment and the card that changed the run. Comparing two different progression states cannot establish that a single spell was better. '+a('damage-meter/','Use the meter carefully')))]
 return dict(id={'warlock':'AS04','hunter':'AS05','priest':'AS06','druid':'AS07','rogue':'AS08','warrior':'AS09','paladin':'AS10','mage':'AS11'}[key],slug='builds/'+key+'/',title=f'Azeroth Survivors {name} Build: Routes & Choices',h1=f'{name} build: choose a route that fits',desc=f'Choose an Azeroth Survivors {name} build by talent state, starting spell and damage triggers, with card priorities and fallbacks for the original game.',answer=d['summary']+ref('game'),parts=parts,related=[('builds/','Compare class build routes'),('best-class/','Choose a class first'),('save-backup/','Keep a save before changing clients')])

def articles():
 pages=[class_page(k) for k in CLASSES]
 pages.append(dict(id='AS02',slug='beginners-guide/',title='Azeroth Survivors Guide: Controls & Your First Run',h1='Start your first Azeroth Survivors run',desc='Open the original Azeroth Survivors, learn the controls and distinguish run upgrades from permanent talents, with checks for WebGPU and loading problems.',answer='Open wow.aethus.pl in a WebGPU-capable browser. Pick a hero, move while spells attack automatically, and choose upgrades when the card offer appears. Keep the cards for this run separate from the talents and equipment you develop between runs.'+ref('game')+ref('launcher'),parts=[
 ('start','From the original page to a run',steps(['Open '+ext('https://wow.aethus.pl/','Aethus’s original game')+'. Keep this guide in a separate tab. The original does not run inside this website.','Allow the initial game-data download to finish. A loading bar is different from a WebGPU warning or a server quota message.','Choose your hero and inspect the class, selected talents and starting spell. A developed character may start with a different spell from a new one.','Start the run with Enter. Move to leave room around the hero, collect experience and read the offered upgrade’s effect before selecting it.','When the run ends, inspect permanent progress and prepare the next attempt. Export a save before changing browser, device or host.'])+para(ref('game')+ref('launcher'))),
 ('controls','The controls you need first',table(['Input','Action','Decision it supports'],[['WASD or both mouse buttons','Move','Leave a route out of the approaching pack.'],['1 / 2 / 3','Choose an offered card','Read the actual card; this is not a fixed shopping list.'],['R','Reroll the offer','Use when the present offer does not support the run; inspect the remaining rerolls in the client.'],['Enter','Play','The original picker’s quick-start prompt.'],['Escape','Pause/menu','Check Options and your current settings.']])+para('These are the original picker and menu prompts, reviewed 29 October 2026. Use Options → Controls / Key Bindings for the current full binding list instead of importing keys from a different reconstruction. '+ref('game'))),
 ('upgrades','Three decisions that should stay separate',table(['Decision','When to make it','What to compare'],[['Run cards','During the level-up offer','The spell you currently use, the trigger it needs and the problem it solves now.'],['Permanent talents','Between runs','Prerequisites, opening-spell changes and the engine you can actually unlock.'],['Permanent equipment','Before comparing another run','Keep the starting investment similar; do not credit the entire difference to one card.']])+para(a('builds/','Find the branch that matches your character'))),
 ('launch-checks','Match a launch problem to the next step',table(['What you see','What to check','What this does not prove'],[['Game-data download','Let the download progress; note whether the counter changes.','A black loading surface alone is not proof of a broken save.'],['No WebGPU warning','Use a current Chrome, Edge or Safari and check GPU availability. The launcher also suggests a Linux Chrome WebGPU flag.','A browser version alone does not guarantee a usable GPU adapter.'],['Too many people are playing','Use the original page’s Windows download or original community link; a quota is not fixed by changing class.','The hidden warning text in HTML is not evidence the server is currently full.'],['Different progress','Return to the previous browser/profile/origin, then export before migrating.','A new host does not automatically inherit old storage.']])+para(ref('launcher')))],related=[('best-class/','Pick a first class'),('save-backup/','Export and protect progress'),('mobile/','Phone and tablet checks')]))
 pages.append(dict(id='AS03',slug='builds/',title='Azeroth Survivors Builds: Choose Your Class Route',h1='Build around the character you have',desc='Compare Azeroth Survivors build routes by class, current talents and failure point. Separate fresh characters, capstone starters and conditional damage.',answer='Choose a class route after checking its current talents and starting spell. Prioritise an engine that already works, then solve the run’s actual failure: crowd clear, boss damage or survival. A finished capstone build is not a fresh-character opening.'+ref('game'),parts=[
 ('routes','Choose a class, then a route',table(['Class','Start before talent changes','Route decision'],[[a('builds/'+k+'/',d['name']),d['start'],d['routes'][0][0]+' versus '+d['routes'][1][0]] for k,d in CLASSES.items()])+para('Shaman is also an original class: its client description emphasises jumping storms and totems. This first set of detailed routes follows the specific class-build tasks investigated for these guides; it does not rank an unreviewed Shaman allocation. '+ref('game'))),
 ('state','Fresh character or developed build?',steps(['Read the selected talent. Does it change the opening spell, add a summon, or create a free cast?','Check whether you can actually afford its prerequisites. A named endpoint is not a complete point-by-point levelling plan.','Choose cards for the present engine. An unavailable endpoint cannot supply its damage during the current run.','After the engine functions, choose the next upgrade for the problem that still ends your runs.'])),
 ('triggers','Read the trigger before the damage number',table(['Trigger','Works when','A misleading comparison'],[['On a kill','You can finish enemies regularly.','Treating a crowded wave as isolated-boss performance.'],['On a critical hit','Relevant attacks actually crit.','Assuming a health-focused setup has the same proc rate.'],['While shielded / when a shield breaks','The stated shield condition holds.','Counting both conditions as permanently active.'],['Periodic free cast','The granting talent is allocated.','Giving a new hero a developed character’s free casts.']])+para('These distinctions come from the original talent text; the priority order is editorial synthesis. No simulated DPS or clear-rate ranking is claimed. '+ref('game'))),
 ('compare','Compare attempts without losing the context',para('Keep the same class, zone, difficulty and permanent investment when judging a change. Then record the engine, one changed choice and the point where the run failed. Use a damage meter to inspect the relevant target and time window, and keep your save file before moving between clients. '+a('damage-meter/','Read DPS windows'))+para('<a href="'+P+'ru/builds/" lang="ru">Билды: выбор маршрута на русском →</a>'))],related=[('best-class/','Choose a first class'),('damage-meter/','Compare damage windows'),('save-backup/','Back up progress')]))
 pages.append(dict(id='AS12',slug='best-class/',title='Azeroth Survivors Best Class: Pick for Your Progress',h1='Which class should you choose?',desc='Choose an Azeroth Survivors class for a fresh save, ranged play, shields or summons. Compare talent conditions without invented damage or win-rate rankings.',answer='For a first melee character, consider Warrior; for a defensive holy route, consider Paladin; for ranged play, consider Hunter. Choose between them by the talents you have unlocked and how you prefer to move. These are editorial kit-based picks, not measured win-rate tiers.'+ref('game'),parts=[
 ('choose','Pick for the job in front of you',table(['Your goal','Start by considering','What to check before deciding'],[['Learn melee crowd fighting',a('builds/warrior/','Warrior'),'Cleave is the baseline; Bladestorm’s free Whirlwinds require the capstone.'],['Build around shields',a('builds/paladin/','Paladin')+' or '+a('builds/priest/','Priest'),'Shield-start changes and shield-break effects need their specific talents.'],['Stay at range',a('builds/hunter/','Hunter'),'Auto Shot before Kill Shot; a developed pet pair is not the default new character.'],['Use summoned attackers',a('builds/warlock/','Warlock')+' or '+a('builds/hunter/','Hunter'),'Check which summon is actually unlocked.'],['Control space with spells',a('builds/mage/','Frost Mage'),'Water Elemental and periodic Frost Nova require the capstone.'],['Switch between ranged and melee directions',a('builds/druid/','Druid'),'Balance and Feral are different plans; Cat and Bear are mutually exclusive.'],['Enjoy conditional melee burst',a('builds/rogue/','Rogue'),'Direct-hit spillover and poison-death chains need different setups.']])+para(ref('game'))),
 ('progress','A tier list needs a progression state',para('A fresh hero, a character with a starting-spell milestone and a fully developed capstone character are three different comparisons. Permanent gear changes survival and damage again. If a guide recommends Hunter for pets, ask whether it means an early wolf or the wolf-and-raptor route. If it recommends Warrior for effortless Whirlwinds, check whether Bladestorm is already allocated.')),
 ('method','How these recommendations are made',para('We compare the original client’s stated attack style, conditional talent engine and opening-spell changes. We do not combine old reconstruction health values with the current original talent tree. We have not measured clear rates or run a controlled damage test, so there is no universal S-to-D performance table. '+ref('game')+ref('rebuild'))+para('If you already have a developed class, fixing its missing trigger or survival problem can be more useful than rerolling to another class at zero progress. '+a('builds/','Choose the route inside your class')))],related=[('beginners-guide/','Begin a first run'),('builds/','Compare build branches'),('damage-meter/','Measure the right window')]))
 pages.extend(support_articles())
 return pages

def support_articles():
 return [dict(id='AS15',slug='save-backup/',title='Azeroth Survivors Save: Export, Import & Backups',h1='Move your save without replacing the wrong progress',desc='Export an Azeroth Survivors save, back up both devices before importing and inspect five local backups. Understand browser storage and replacement limits.',answer='In the original game, open Options → Saves and export a .sav file before changing browser or device. Import replaces the destination’s progress; it does not merge two runs. Export the destination too if you want to keep both branches.'+ref('game')+ref('saves'),parts=[
 ('export','Make a copy before changing anything',steps(['Return to the original browser, profile and game address where the progress exists.','Open Options → Saves → Export Save. Keep the original .sav file unchanged.','Name your own backup folder by date and note the game version. Do not edit the file to make a rejected import look valid.','If the destination already has progress, export that separately before selecting Import Save there.'])+para('The save bridge creates a dated AzerothSurvivors .sav download. Client text says the file carries heroes, each class’s opened zones, gear, talents and Codex progress. '+ref('saves')+ref('game'))),
 ('import','Import, then check the result',steps(['Transfer a copy of the file to the other device yourself.','Open Options → Saves → Import Save in the intended destination browser.','Read the replacement warning and confirm only if this is the branch you want there.','Inspect the hero, opened zones, equipment and talents before deleting either backup.'])+para('The bridge only hands file text to the game; the client validates it. We have not tested every cross-version import, so a rejected file is a reason to keep the original and compare versions, not to alter its contents. '+ref('saves'))),
 ('recover','If progress is missing',table(['Situation','First place to look','Boundary'],[['Different browser/profile/device','The earlier browser and profile on the original address.','Storage is not automatically the same across clients.'],['A recent mistake','Options → Saves → Backups.','The current text describes hourly play backups, retaining five; these are local copies.'],['Old mirror or framed page','Its own export/recovery control, if present.','The original launcher contains a fallback export for a stored save or newest backup. This guide cannot access another site’s storage.'],['Cleared storage and no export','Any file backup you already kept.','We cannot reconstruct missing progress or guarantee recovery.']])+para(ref('game')+ref('launcher')))],related=[('mobile/','Move to a phone carefully'),('beginners-guide/','Return to the original game'),('addons/','Addon storage is separate')]),
 dict(id='AS13',slug='addons/',title='Azeroth Survivors Addons: Browser & Desktop Setup',h1='Install an addon in the right client',desc='Install Azeroth Survivors addon ZIPs in the browser or a matching desktop folder. Check author downloads, folder names, loading and local storage limits.',answer='In the browser, use Options → AddOns → Install AddOns and select the author’s ZIP. On desktop, use the AddOns folder opened by the game and match the folder name to its .toc file. Browser installation and desktop extraction are different paths.'+ref('game')+ref('addons'),parts=[
 ('choose','Choose the smallest tool that answers your question',table(['Need','First option','Why'],[['Only total damage','The built-in damage meter','No community package needed.'],['Per-spell damage and DPS windows','AZS Spell Meter','The author documents spell rows, proc attribution and configurable windows.'],['A complete HUD replacement','Check the original author’s compatibility notes','A replacement UI changes more than a single measurement window.']])+para(ext('https://github.com/kex0/AZSSpellMeter/releases/latest','GitHub · AZS Spell Meter releases')+' — use the author’s release, then read its requirements. '+ref('meter'))),
 ('browser','Browser: keep the ZIP intact',steps(['Download the chosen addon ZIP from its author.','Open the original game’s Options → AddOns → Install AddOns.','Choose the ZIP and inspect the installed entry; enable the addon in the list.','Start the next run so the game can load it. Install an updated ZIP through the same menu when the author releases one.'])+para('The browser installer stores files in IndexedDB for that browser and origin. They do not automatically follow the save file to a second device; clearing site storage can remove them. '+ref('addons'))),
 ('desktop','Desktop: check the directory level',steps(['Open Options → AddOns → Open AddOns Folder in the downloaded game.','Extract the author’s addon into that folder. For AZS Spell Meter the author documents AddOns/AZSSpellMeter/AZSSpellMeter.toc.','If the extracted directory is AZSSpellMeter-main or has another wrapper folder, rename or move the actual addon folder so its name matches the .toc.','Relog as the addon author instructs, then check the addon entry again.'])+para(ref('meter'))),
 ('missing','If it is missing, outdated or invisible',table(['Symptom','Check','Next step'],[['Not in the desktop list','Folder nesting and .toc name.','Correct the directory before downloading a different package.'],['Not present in a second browser','Where you originally installed the ZIP.','Install there separately; importing a game save is not an addon transfer.'],['Out of date','The addon’s interface/version and current author release.','The game offers Load out of date AddOns but warns compatibility may fail.'],['AZS meter offscreen','Saved window position.','Use /azsm resetpos; see the meter guide for view settings.']])+para('Optional native helpers such as DLL updaters are separate from Lua addon files and cannot be assumed to run in the browser. This guide does not require installing a native helper. '+ref('addons')+ref('meter')+ref('game')))],related=[('damage-meter/','Set up and interpret the meter'),('save-backup/','Keep progress before moving clients'),('mobile/','Browser and device differences')]),
 dict(id='AS14',slug='damage-meter/',title='Azeroth Survivors Damage Meter: Setup & DPS Windows',h1='Turn on the meter, then compare the right numbers',desc='Enable the Azeroth Survivors damage meter. Compare damage, boss views and AZS Spell Meter DPS windows without confusing procs or different run states.',answer='Open Options and enable Show Damage Meter for the built-in meter. Add AZS Spell Meter only if you need its per-spell views and configurable DPS window. A ten-second DPS number and a whole-run average answer different questions.'+ref('game')+ref('meter'),parts=[
 ('built-in','Start with the built-in meter',steps(['Open Options and find Show Damage Meter in the HUD/interface settings.','Enable it, then use the meter’s minimap button or window.','Adjust HUD Scale if it is too small; Damage Meter on Top controls whether it stays over upgrade cards.','Select the view that matches the question: total damage, healing, boss damage or party output.'])+para('Client messages include “No damage yet”, “No healing yet” and “Only in a party”. An empty view before its relevant event is not by itself an addon failure. '+ref('game'))),
 ('window','Choose a measurement window',table(['Question','Useful view/window','Keep constant'],[['Did this change improve recent wave clear?','A recent DPS window','Compare the same minute, difficulty and starting investment.'],['What dealt the most across the run?','Whole-run damage/share','Run duration; a longer attempt has more time to accumulate damage.'],['What reached the boss?','Boss view','The same boss and similar gear/talents.'],['Which effect created a proc’s damage?','Per-spell row and proc breakdown','The addon version and grouping method.']])+para('kex0 documents a default ten-second window, configurable settings and a “Since the start” average. The author also groups proc damage under the spell actually cast; a different row label can reflect attribution rather than missing damage. '+ref('meter'))),
 ('addon','When using AZS Spell Meter',para(a('addons/','Install the author’s addon')+' first. Commands documented by the author are <code>/azsm</code> to show/hide, <code>/azsm resetpos</code> to restore position and <code>/azsm lock</code> to lock dragging. The title-bar settings control the DPS window and columns. While an addon window is open, its author says the built-in Damage Done meter is hidden; closing all addon views restores it if it was enabled. '+ref('meter'))),
 ('compare','Do not promote one number into a tier list',para('Record class, capstone, zone, difficulty, permanent gear and time before comparing two readings. A kill-triggered build in a dense wave and a shield build against a lone boss are not the same experiment. An impressive screenshot does not establish the best class for a fresh save. '+a('builds/','Check each build’s trigger'))+para('The author reports v1.32 tested with game 0.123.0. We inspected the original 0.127.0 text, but have not run a compatibility benchmark with that addon; check the latest author release if a view behaves differently. '+ref('meter')))],related=[('addons/','Install or update an addon'),('builds/','Compare conditional build routes'),('best-class/','Choose a class by goal')]),
 dict(id='AS16',slug='mobile/',title='Azeroth Survivors Mobile: Browser & Save Checks',h1='Check the phone route before moving your save',desc='Check Azeroth Survivors mobile browser requirements, WebGPU, input and storage. Separate original-browser access from device-specific Winlator reports.',answer='Try the original wow.aethus.pl in a current WebGPU-capable browser on your phone or tablet. A browser name or OS version alone does not guarantee a usable graphics adapter or successful play. Export your existing save before switching clients.'+ref('launcher'),parts=[
 ('route','Choose between two different routes',table(['Route','What it uses','Evidence limit'],[['Original browser page','The phone browser, its GPU access and the game’s input handling.','Launcher/client support is not a tested-device compatibility list.'],['Windows build through Winlator','A Windows build and a community compatibility layer on Android.','One public player reports success; no universal configuration or performance guarantee is established here.']])+para('The Winlator report is by Reddit user starsforfeelings; other replies report mixed browser outcomes. Its indexed and displayed dates disagree, so we do not assign it an exact publication date. '+ref('mobile'))),
 ('checks','Browser checks, in order',steps(['Open '+ext('https://wow.aethus.pl/','Aethus’s original game')+' directly, outside an embedded frame.','If the page reports no WebGPU, update the browser and inspect whether the device exposes the required GPU feature. Do not use a PC-only flag as a blanket phone fix.','Let the initial download complete; note whether its progress counter moves. A server quota message is a different branch from a GPU warning.','Inspect the actual touch/input controls before committing to a long run. A larger display does not prove that all inputs work on your device.','If the original browser route is unsuitable, retain the PC save and check current original-author/community guidance for your device. Do not install a purported mobile port just because it uses the game’s name.'])+para(ref('launcher')+ref('game'))),
 ('saves','Your PC and phone do not share storage automatically',para('Export from the client where your progress exists; export any phone progress separately before importing. Import replaces the destination. Keep both original files until heroes, equipment and zone unlocks match your intention. Browser addon installation is separate again. '+ref('saves')+ref('addons'))+para(a('save-backup/','Follow the full backup and migration order'))),
 ('limits','What has and has not been checked',para('We inspected the original launcher and client text and read the public mobile report. We have not completed a run on a physical Android phone, iPhone or iPad, benchmarked Winlator, or verified every cross-version save transfer. Device model, GPU, browser, game version and the exact warning are more useful troubleshooting details than “mobile does not work”.'))],related=[('save-backup/','Export before switching devices'),('beginners-guide/#launch-checks','Separate loading warnings'),('addons/','Reinstall browser addons separately')])]

def russian():
 rows=[['Воин',a('builds/warrior/','Fury / Protection'),'Whirlwind с Bladestorm или здоровье и Shield Slam с Titan. Начальный Cleave не означает, что финальный талант уже открыт.'],['Паладин',a('builds/paladin/','Protection / Retribution'),'Щиты и максимальное здоровье либо критические срабатывания Exorcism. Урон при действующем щите отличается от урона при его разрушении.'],['Охотник',a('builds/hunter/','Marksmanship / Beast Mastery'),'Auto Shot по умолчанию; Kill Shot меняет начало на Aimed Shot. Второй питомец требует соответствующего таланта.'],['Жрец',a('builds/priest/','Discipline / Shadow'),'Выбирайте между поддержанием щита и распространением Shadow Word: Pain после смерти цели.'],['Друид',a('builds/druid/','Balance / Feral'),'Повторный Starfire либо ближний бой в форме. Cat Form и Dire Bear Form нельзя складывать вместе.'],['Разбойник',a('builds/rogue/','Combat / Assassination'),'Прямые удары по соседним целям либо облака после смерти отравленных или кровоточащих врагов.'],['Маг',a('builds/mage/','Fire / Frost / Arcane'),'Огненные взрывы требуют убийств; ледяной элементаль и периодическая Frost Nova требуют финального таланта.'],['Чернокнижник',a('builds/warlock/','Affliction / Demonology'),'Периодический урон с распространением либо призывы. Seed of Corruption меняет начальное заклинание.']]
 return dict(id='AS18',slug='ru/builds/',lang='ru',title='Билды Azeroth Survivors: выбор по талантам',h1='Выберите билд под текущего героя',desc='Билды Azeroth Survivors для оригинала Aethus: ветки талантов, начальные заклинания, условия срабатывания и выбор улучшений без выдуманного рейтинга урона.',answer='Сначала проверьте выбранные таланты и начальное заклинание, затем выбирайте улучшения для уже работающего механизма. Новый герой и герой с финальным талантом начинают по-разному. Здесь сравниваются условия сборок, а не измеренные проценты побед.'+ref('game'),parts=[
 ('routes','Какую ветку выбрать',table(['Класс','Подробный маршрут на английском','Что проверить'],rows)),
 ('order','Порядок решений во время забега',steps(['Посмотрите, какое заклинание уже есть у героя. Не рассчитывайте на эффект ещё не открытого таланта.','Выберите главный механизм: прямые удары, периодический урон, питомцы, щиты или контроль.','Поддерживайте его подходящими картами. Для эффекта после убийства нужна смерть цели; попадание само по себе недостаточно.','Определите, что мешает: слабый урон по боссу, плотная толпа или недостаток выживаемости. Следующее улучшение должно решать именно эту проблему.','Сравнивайте попытки с одинаковыми зоной, сложностью и постоянным снаряжением.'])),
 ('terms','Термины и границы этой таблицы',para('Имена талантов и заклинаний оставлены на английском рядом с русским объяснением, чтобы их можно было найти при смене языка клиента. «Финальный талант» здесь обозначает capstone, который может менять начало забега. Список веток — не полная раскладка очков и не гарантированный порядок выпадения карт. Русские строки оригинального клиента проверены отдельно от старой реконструкции. '+ref('game'))+para('В исходных текстах некоторых эффектов числа заданы шаблоном. Мы не подставляем выдуманные значения и не складываем несовместимые формы или условия. Проверка основана на тексте версии 0.127.0 от 29 октября 2026 года; собственный игровой тест этих сборок не проводился.')),
 ('save','Перед сменой устройства сохраните прогресс',para('В оригинале откройте Options → Saves → Export Save. На другом устройстве Import Save заменяет текущий прогресс, поэтому сначала экспортируйте и его. Сохранение из другого браузера не появляется автоматически. '+ref('saves')+ref('game')))],related=[('builds/','English: all build decisions'),('damage-meter/','English: DPS windows'),('save-backup/','English: save transfer')])
